  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.20 Fire suppression system",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.20 “Fire suppression system” means a system which is used to extinguish, control, or in some cases, entirely prevent fires from spreading or occurring and includes, but are not limited to fire sprinkler heads, water piping networks, standpipes, and smoke alarms.\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
